{
  "core_question": "How to design a defensible first version of an AI sepsis‑risk decision support tool covering clinical safety, legal/regulatory exposure, and financial structure for a 12‑hospital system",
  "rationale": "Clinical safety requires evidence‑based validation and workflow integration; legal/regulatory expertise is needed to navigate FDA SaMD, HIPAA, and liability issues; finance must address subscription economics, reimbursement, and ROI.",
  "routes": ["healthcare", "legal", "finance"],
  "sub_questions": {
    "healthcare": "For a 12‑hospital health system deploying an AI sepsis risk score in the EHR on a per‑seat annual subscription model, what clinical safety measures should be included in version 1? Include validation study design, performance metrics (sensitivity, specificity, AUROC), bias mitigation steps, real‑time monitoring protocols, and integration points with existing sepsis care pathways.",
    "legal": "Given the same deployment scenario, what legal and regulatory requirements must be addressed for a defensible first release of an AI clinical decision support tool? Cover FDA SaMD classification and premarket pathway, CLIA compliance if applicable, HIPAA privacy safeguards, data governance, informed consent considerations, liability risk mitigation, and any relevant state or federal statutes.",
    "finance": "For the 12‑hospital system using a per‑seat annual subscription for an AI sepsis risk score tool, what financial structure should be designed to ensure defensibility? Outline pricing strategy, cost allocation (development, maintenance, compliance), reimbursement options (e.g., CMS ICD‑10 codes or bundled payments), ROI calculation, and risk mitigation mechanisms such as performance guarantees or penalty clauses."
  },
  "requires_recency_disclosure": true,
  "recency_notes": "Potentially stale FDA SaMD guidance updates post‑2024, recent CMS sepsis bundle reimbursement changes, evolving sepsis clinical guidelines, and new state privacy laws."
}
